==Battleground==
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[R.Ost]]s spawn after 153.33 seconds<sup>4,600f</sup>, delay 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Master A.]] spawns after 153.33 seconds<sup>4,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 2~12 seconds<sup>60f~360f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Your main goal is to try and kill each R.Ost as fast as possible, as even two of them stacking can result in a loss. This isn't mentioning the Master A. that spawns in later that can pick off your meatshields from a safe distance, further crippling any defense you created to stall R.Ost. A Rich Cat is recommended due to minor cash flow, unless your units are strong enough to push through R.Ost.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Magica Cat]]: Magica's Weaken is very strong here, drastically reducing R.Ost's pushing power. If you have access to [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Driller]], you can weaken R.Ost '''and''' Master A. (by using R.Ost as a stepping stone) by 90% instead!
*[[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]]: Make sure that your attackers have over 260 range. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] just barely outranges R.Ost. [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] is a great option on this stage, though try not to spam her or you'll lose money fast.
*[[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]]: Dragon Cat has good range and helps for R.Ost chipping. If you have [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon]], stack both Dragons.
*[[:Category:Backliner-class Cats|Backliners]]: As per usual, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] are good for the R.Osts. Time Bahamut so he doesn't accidentally target Trolly Blogger.
*[[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Wall]]: This elusive gacha unit will be of great help thanks to his Resistance to Traitless, allowing him to wall R.Ost in place, especially if aided by research [[Cat Combo]]s.
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: A great meatshield for this stage that fulfills a similar role to Brainwashed Wall. However, you can actually use this cat in {{4c}} difficulties.

